## Developer execution envelope

{% set development_budget_minutes = DEVELOPMENT_BUDGET_MINUTES|default('unknown', true) %}
{% set development_worker_cap = DEVELOPMENT_MAX_PARALLEL_WORKERS|default('1', true) %}

The implementation plan must fit the developer's actual execution context:

{% if development_budget_minutes != 'unknown' %}
- the complete development phase has {{ development_budget_minutes }} minutes
  before its timebox ends; retries and loopbacks consume the same budget, so a
  continuation receives only the remaining time;
{% else %}
- no numerical development timebox is configured, so the plan must state that
  execution fit is not numerically evaluable and use self-contained units;
{% endif %}
- at most {{ development_worker_cap }} concurrent sub-agents may run in parallel;
- integration, full verification, and artifact submission must finish inside
  that development-phase budget.

Size each unit so one sub-agent can understand, implement, and run its focused
proof from a self-contained context packet without exhausting one agent
context. That packet must name the objective, owned paths, dependencies already
satisfied, relevant request and plan references, and focused proof. Use
delegation to keep discovery and unit implementation out of the developer agent's main-session
context, and keep sub-agent returns compact enough for fan-in: changed files,
commands and outcomes, unresolved risks, and no raw discovery transcript.

Estimate the critical path, including waves forced by the sub-agent cap and real
dependencies, not the sum of parallel branches. Reserve explicit developer agent
time and context for fan-in, conflict repair, full verification, and artifact
submission. The plan is acceptable only when it is divided and parallelized
enough for that critical path plus the reserve to fit inside the
development-phase budget. Keep splitting independent work until the developer
can walk the manifest, dispatch subagents wave by wave, and finish on time. The
total workload may be much larger than one agent could finish sequentially;
judge the bounded critical path, not total size or subjective confidence. Do not invent a token
count: the runtime does not expose one here, so use the bounded phase budget,
self-contained sub-agent packets, and bounded return summaries as the context-fit
constraints.
